# Git commit & push safety

## Never commit

- `.env` and any credential / secret files
- `backend/uploads/` (user/CMS/product media — local only)
- Temporary debug scripts under `backend/scripts/` unless the user explicitly asks (e.g. `checkRefunds.js`, `retryRefund.js`, `testCouponCategory.js`, `_tmp*.js`)
- `node_modules/`, `dist/`, `build/`, lockfiles already ignored

## Do commit (when the user asks)

- App source: `src/`, `backend/controllers|models|routes|services|utils|config|middleware`
- Real feature scripts the user wants shared (e.g. one-off migrations they approve)
- `.cursor/rules/` when adding project conventions

## Commit / push habits

- Only commit when the user explicitly asks
- Only push when the user explicitly asks
- Prefer clear, why-focused commit messages
- Keep `$0.01` Waafi test pricing unless the user changes it
- Do not force-push `main`/`master`

## If unsure

Ask before adding large binaries, uploads, or one-off test scripts.
